From 5142bfa6b386f04b085867e6a7eb4ef35e869ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:16:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 171/171] wifi: mt6797: bind the directed Action discard class
 to the key state (its keyed descriptor variant)

Runtime 24 (candidate 23, compile 28) completed the pairwise key command with
message 4 in flight (the credit waiter's ownership of proposal 0170 observed),
discarded the runtime 21 and runtime 17 classes, and then fail-stopped at the
receive-frame gate on a frame of runtime 18's directed clear Action class: 136 bytes,
type word 0xee01, unicast-to-me match, BSSID field 1, WLAN index 1, frame
control 0x00d0, receiver this station and transmitter the target, with two
descriptor fields changed from runtime 18: byte 9 0x40 and status 0xe004
where runtime 18, before any key, carried 0 and 0xe000.

Pinned public layout: byte 9's upper nibble is the security mode (4 is CCMP)
and bit 2 of the status word is RX_STATUS_FLAG_CIPHER_MISMATCH; the ICV-error
flag (bit 4) is clear. Inference, not measured: once the pairwise key is
installed under WLAN entry 1, the descriptor reports that entry's cipher
context and an unprotected frame received on it is flagged as a cipher
mismatch. The decoder now admits the keyed variant (exactly 0x40 and 0xe004)
only when the caller passes that the pairwise key is installed, and keeps
admitting runtime 18's unkeyed variant (exactly 0 and 0xe000) at every stage
it already did; the keyed variant before the key and every mixed pair are not
the class. The frame stays a discard within the same eight-per-join budget
and is never delivered; every other condition, window and budget is
unchanged. "Same class" means the same source-defined frame class: no body or
sequence was retained in either run, and the category, body, BSSID and
sequence are not claimed.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
